Dialogue: 0,1:17:26.83,1:17:33.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would use a dipole with only two tiny little pieces of light here.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:33.83,1:17:41.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I would now have great contrast in this direction and 0 contrast in the other direction.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:41.17,1:17:45.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the only thing that I can now do is print lines that are infinitely long.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:45.95,1:17:49.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not a single designer is interested in that.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:49.03,1:17:55.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So now what you could do is well, but if I have those very long lines, I will use a second exposure to cut them.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:55.59,1:17:57.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,But that's expensive.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:57.01,1:18:01.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perhaps bring in these poles a little bit, regain a little bit of that contrast.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:01.33,1:18:06.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And now I can also print gaps in these lines.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:06.35,1:18:08.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,But how small I can get that gap.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:08.85,1:18:17.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's the so-called tip to tip difference that depends on how you optimize the illumination and how you optimize the OPC.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:17.29,1:18:21.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's a very interactive discussion between us and our customers.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:21.85,1:18:23.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hope that answers your question.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:23.47,1:18:24.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,OK, here's another question.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:24.83,1:18:26.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just a quick question.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:26.35,1:18:40.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if the minimum pitch you're expecting is like 90 nanometers, that does bring up the question, what exactly does the metric in like a node name refer to.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:40.31,1:18:44.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Because it's clearly not the pitch of the features themselves.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:44.73,1:18:45.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great question.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:45.87,1:18:52.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah so the node names right 5 nanometer node, 4 nanometer node three nanometer node.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.61,1:19:00.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Back in the days that we had the 45 nanometer node that actually really represented the size of the lines.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:00.57,1:19:04.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,And at some point that became very increasingly difficult.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:04.77,1:19:16.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But people also became very creative in terms of with design tricks and layout tricks, I can get more density out of the size that I have.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:16.87,1:19:26.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So think of the 5 nanometer and the 4 nanometer and 3 nanometer now more as an indication of what is the effective transistor density.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:26.77,1:19:32.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,How many transistors can I get per squared per square millimeter or per square micron.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:32.67,1:19:37.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's more an indication of that instead of really the dimension.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:37.45,1:19:39.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Tony, anything you would like to add.
